<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:p1="clr-namespace:;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:dev="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns:aud="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Audio;assembly=OpenRigs.Audio"
                 xmlns:dsp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Dsp;assembly=Bonsai.Dsp"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>The domes' preflight, run from rig-control's Preflight page and card as the test mouse: the domes' rig list (OpenRigs.Devices DomeHardware) opens and readies every device as a task does, no experiment folder (NoExperimentFolder), and the lab's check (OpenRigs.Devices PreflightChecks) counts each rig.yml device from its piece's data (Taps) and, from Go, writes the raw rows to RawFile with the questions of TaskPath (config\task-dome.yml). A device that fails as it opens stops the preflight naming it, as it stops a task. Pulse and Reset on BehaviorBoard-Main are the board's ManualPulses piece; the spouts move by the lick spout stage's own commands. Each rig.yml speaker plays a test sound while its question is asked (SpeakerTest), and the projector shows a test pattern (TestPattern). coen_qc_preflight_rig.judge applies the thresholds.</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" Description="The folder holding &lt;MACHINE&gt;\rig.yml, read by ReadLabRig; a launch property. LiveView keeps its own ConfigRoot: an edge into it makes Bonsai build it before the pieces, and it then streams nothing." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
        <Description>This machine's rig.yml (ConfigRoot\MACHINE\rig.yml) read once into the lab rig model: RigConfigs, RigFile, RigConfigDirectory and ConfigRoot, which every device piece reads. First, before anything that reads them.</Description>
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:NoExperimentFolder.bonsai">
        <SubjectId>_preflight_</SubjectId>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
        <Property Name="LaunchId" Description="The launcher's run id; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl, TCP 5561 on this machine), with no commands of its own: Pulse and Reset are the board's ManualPulses', Confirm is PreflightChecks' and the spouts' are the lick spout stage's. EndAfterStop ends headless Bonsai when it is still running 2 s after the controller's stop.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
              <Property Name="LaunchId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <LaunchId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters />
              <Commands />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Description>Ends headless Bonsai when it is still running 2 s after the controller's stop: the live view's publisher threads keep the process alive until every device's teardown reaches them, and one held up kept Bonsai running until the agent's kill 30 s after End Testing (GREEN-DOME-2, 15 Nov 2026). Nothing in the editor.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:EndAfterStop">
                <orcl:GraceSeconds>2</orcl:GraceSeconds>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="DisplayDevice" DisplayName="DisplayDevice" Description="The display the dome projector is on (DomeHardware's ProjectorDisplay); a launch property, as in the dome tasks. First by default, the display the lab's dome windows open on." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The domes' rig list (OpenRigs.Devices DomeHardware), as in every dome task: each piece from its rig.yml entry, opened and readied, Ready from its ReadyGate; and the board's ManualPulses (Pulse and Reset).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="DisplayDevice" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:DomeHardware.bonsai">
              <DisplayDevice>First</DisplayDevice>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.ManualPulses.bonsai">
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="RawFile" Description="Where the raw rows go; a launch property." />
        <Property Name="TaskPath" Description="The task file app-rig-control writes at Go: config\task-dome.yml with the form's edits." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:PreflightChecks.bonsai">
        <RawFile>preflight-raw.csv</RawFile>
        <TaskPath>..\config\task-dome.yml</TaskPath>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Taps</Name>
        <Description>Each device piece's data, and the projector's frames (DrawStimuli), as the check's ticks (OpenRigs.Devices PreflightTap into DeviceTicks), by the device's rig.yml name.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TimestampGeneratorGen3-Main.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PreflightTap">
                <dev:Device>TimestampGeneratorGen3-Main</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>DeviceTicks</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PreflightTap">
                <dev:Device>BehaviorBoard-Main</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>DeviceTicks</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LicketySplit-Left.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PreflightTap">
                <dev:Device>LicketySplit-Left</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>DeviceTicks</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LicketySplit-Right.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PreflightTap">
                <dev:Device>LicketySplit-Right</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>DeviceTicks</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>StepperDriver-A.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PreflightTap">
                <dev:Device>StepperDriver-A</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>DeviceTicks</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>StepperDriver-B.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PreflightTap">
                <dev:Device>StepperDriver-B</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>DeviceTicks</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Camera-Face.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PreflightTap">
                <dev:Device>Camera-Face</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>DeviceTicks</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Camera-Pupil.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PreflightTap">
                <dev:Device>Camera-Pupil</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>DeviceTicks</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Camera-Body.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PreflightTap">
                <dev:Device>Camera-Body</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>DeviceTicks</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>DrawStimuli</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dev:PreflightTap">
                <dev:Device>ProjectionCalibration</dev:Device>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>DeviceTicks</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="22" To="23" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="24" To="25" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="25" To="26" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="27" To="28" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="28" To="29" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>SpeakerTest</Name>
        <Description>A test sound for each rig.yml speaker, laid out by OpenRigs.Audio SpeakerBuffer on that speaker's channel alone, equalised, at the lab's default level (SpeakerBuffer's LevelDbfs, -30 dBFS RMS), through DomeHardware's mixer. Once the check asks "SpeakerArray: ..." (CheckEvents), the speakers play their test sound in rig.yml's order, one after another, every 5 s until the person's Confirm for SpeakerArray (PreflightChecks' Confirms); each sound the mixer is sent is counted for its speaker (CountSpeakerSounds into SpeakerSounds: the devices metric and the raw rows). The test sound is a 0.3 s 1 kHz tone then 0.3 s of silence (Bonsai.Dsp FunctionGenerator at 48 kHz).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dsp:FunctionGenerator">
                <dsp:BufferLength>14400</dsp:BufferLength>
                <dsp:Frequency>1000</dsp:Frequency>
                <dsp:Waveform>Sine</dsp:Waveform>
                <dsp:SampleRate>48000</dsp:SampleRate>
                <dsp:Depth>F32</dsp:Depth>
                <dsp:Amplitude>1</dsp:Amplitude>
                <dsp:Offset>0</dsp:Offset>
                <dsp:Phase>0</dsp:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dsp:FunctionGenerator">
                <dsp:BufferLength>14400</dsp:BufferLength>
                <dsp:Frequency>1000</dsp:Frequency>
                <dsp:Waveform>Sine</dsp:Waveform>
                <dsp:SampleRate>48000</dsp:SampleRate>
                <dsp:Depth>F32</dsp:Depth>
                <dsp:Amplitude>0</dsp:Amplitude>
                <dsp:Offset>0</dsp:Offset>
                <dsp:Phase>0</dsp:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dsp:Concat">
                <dsp:Axis>1</dsp:Axis>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TestTone</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Speakers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Speakers</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>TestSound</Name>
              <Description>One speaker's test sound: SpeakerBuffer on its channel alone, equalised for it, at the lab's default level.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Channel</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:ToArray" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Speakers</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TestTone</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Channels" Selector="Item1" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                    <Selector>Item2</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="aud:SpeakerBuffer">
                      <aud:Channels />
                      <aud:LevelDbfs>-30</aud:LevelDbfs>
                      <aud:Equalise>true</aud:Equalise>
                      <aud:SyncCopy>false</aud:SyncCopy>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:ToList" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TestSounds</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>CheckEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>SpeakersAsked?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Prompt != null &amp;&amp; Prompt.StartsWith("SpeakerArray:")</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>PlayUntilAnswered</Name>
              <Description>Every speaker's test sound, sent together: the mixer plays them one after another (AppendBuffer queues each behind the last); again every 5 s until the person's Confirm for SpeakerArray after Go.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Timer">
                      <rx:DueTime>PT0S</rx:DueTime>
                      <rx:Period>PT5S</rx:Period>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Confirms</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="dev:Answered">
                      <dev:Device>SpeakerArray</dev:Device>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TestSounds</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item2</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>StimulusSounds</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="2" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>MixerStimulusSounds</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Description>The evidence the speakers were played to: each sound the mixer is sent (past SpeakerMixer's CheckMixerStarted, on its way to AppendBuffer) counted for every rig.yml speaker whose channel carries sound in it, a stderr line each (preflight: SpeakerArray left test sound 1 sent to the mixer).</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="p1:CountSpeakerSounds" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>SpeakerSounds</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="18" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TestPattern</Name>
        <Description>A white rectangle over the whole of DomeHardware's projector view (ProjectorDisplay's azimuth -135 to 135 and elevation -22.5 to 82.5 degrees: 270 by 105, centred at 0, 30), drawn on DrawStimuli from Start until the stop, for the question "Does the test pattern fill the screen?".</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>DrawStimuli</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawQuad.bonsai">
              <ExtentX>270</ExtentX>
              <ExtentY>105</ExtentY>
              <LocationX>0</LocationX>
              <LocationY>30</LocationY>
              <Layer>0</Layer>
              <Angle>0</Angle>
              <ColorR>1</ColorR>
              <ColorG>1</ColorG>
              <ColorB>1</ColorB>
              <ColorA>1</ColorA>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="lv:StreamDevices">
        <Name>LiveView</Name>
        <Description>Streams every rig.yml device the pieces publish (their &lt;Device&gt;.Data) to rig-control's live view (OpenRigs.LiveView): data on TCP 5556, video on 5558. No experiment folder, so the session key stays ready. Last in the workflow: it finds only subjects built before it.</Description>
        <lv:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</lv:ConfigRoot>
        <lv:DataPort>5556</lv:DataPort>
        <lv:VideoPort>5558</lv:VideoPort>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
